 "text": "Hey, good to hear from you. How are you? I lean towards matte, it feels less flashy and keeps the focus on the photo. How about a middle ground, a glossy finish with matte around it? Sounds like they' worth it. Sure thing. It' not overly cold, but dress in layers and keep a window open. The living room across the hall is warmer. Set her up in there if she comes. Probably, it's worth asking her. Some gas fires do, try turning it off before you sit near it. Then hung the photo bag in there instead of her. Nice one, back to you in a moment. Good, lead with the living room for now. I had bronchitis, it hurts. So, the living room it is, for now. Keep the window open and ask your grandmother to sit in there.",
